Subject: [PATCH] virgl: also take the vtest socket from MESA_VTEST_SOCKET_NAME

The Launcher engine gives a Wine process only the variables it knows (src/wine_environment.rs:
MESA_*, GALLIUM_*, VK_*, LIBGL_* and the other graphics prefixes, not VTEST_*), so
VTEST_SOCKET_NAME never reaches the game's virgl driver (GALLIUM_DRIVER=virpipe), which then
connects to /tmp/.virgl_test, a path that Android does not have. When VTEST_SOCKET_NAME is not
set, take MESA_VTEST_SOCKET_NAME, which the engine passes on, as patches/mesa-sysdrv/0001 does
for Venus.

---
--- a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_socket.c
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_socket.c
@@ -201,6 +201,9 @@
    struct sockaddr_un un;
    int sock, ret;
    const char* socket_name = os_get_option("VTEST_SOCKET_NAME");
+   /* PD2 Launcher: the engine passes MESA_* variables to Wine processes, not VTEST_* */
+   if (!socket_name)
+      socket_name = os_get_option("MESA_VTEST_SOCKET_NAME");
 
    sock = socket(PF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0);
    if (sock < 0)
